---
savestate
-- saves your previous directory with a reminder message in pure sh
---
Usage
-- add `eval "$(savestate/resume '<NAME>')"` to your shell rc/profile
---- NAME can be set to __last to use the last savestate
------ eval is needed for `cd` to work
---
Compatibility
-- tested in oksh, dash, bash & zsh
---- bash & dash seem to have issues with eval unless the subshell is properly quoted
---- this is likely due to $IFS nonsense
  >> .profile was used for oksh/dash and .bashrc/.zshrc for bash/zsh
---
